Ravana questions angry Shurpanakha about Rama --- Shurpanakha describes long-armed large-eyed Rama like Kandarpa --- Shurpanakha describes tireless bowman felling fourteen thousand single-handed --- Shurpanakha tells lone survival spared from woman-killing scruple --- Shurpanakha praises devoted valiant Lakshmana as Rama's outer life --- Shurpanakha praises peerless Sita outliving Indra's bliss --- Shurpanakha tells attempted seizure for Ravana's wife --- Shurpanakha urges killing brothers and enjoying widowed Sita